WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.300
-As most Republicans

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.534
fully embrace Donald Trump,

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.367
others are trying
to have it both ways

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:06.501
by courting his base

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:08.901
while keeping Trump himself
at arm's length.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:10.534
Meanwhile, Trump is
still trying to cover up

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:12.801
what happened behind
the scenes on January 6th.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.767
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:19.234
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:22.100
President Biden is currently
on a major international trip,

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.634
where he just completed
a G20 Summit in Rome

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:25.801
and then headed to Glasgow

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.767
for a conference
on climate change

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.901
and, as his poll numbers sag
here at home,

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.734
he seems invigorated
by the trip,

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:34.133
as evidenced by this headline
in The New York Times...

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:40.467
Well, I'm glad
you're having fun.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:41.901
[ Laughter ]
Meanwhile, we're all stuck here

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:43.501
with our weird aunt and uncle.

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:44.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:45.734
"You kids want some dinner?

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.767
Well, how are you going
to pay for it?!"

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:51.634
Biden's like a divorcée
posting Facebook photos

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.367
from a solo trip to Europe.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:55.167
Next, he's going
to post a pic on Insta

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.634
from a gondola in Venice,

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:58.067
wearing a sun hat
with the caption...

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:02.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:04.300
But, hey, we've all been there.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.501
You're stressed,
having a tough time at work,

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:08.133
so you grab a pint
of Haagen-Dazs

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:09.467
and you call up your best bud --

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:11.033
in Biden's case, Obama --
and say --

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:12.200
[ As Biden ]
I just need a reset.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.667
And he says --
[ As Obama ] Uh...when I'm down,

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:18.067
I find it always helps
to do a podcast with, uh...

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:20.334
Bruce Springsteen.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:21.701
And then, you mutter
under your breath,

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.200
"Well, we're not all you."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.467
So you say, "Eff it."
You pack a bag.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.701
You head to the airport,
buy the first ticket to Italy,

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:30.434
where you eat, you pray,
and, most importantly...

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:34.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.467
Of course, when Trump went
abroad, it was more like...

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:42.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:44.834
[ As Johnny Carson ]
Eat, pray, shove.

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:46.767
Eat, pray, shove.

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:47.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.634
Did you, uh,

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:50.767
did you like that one, Wally?

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.701
[ As Ed McMahon ]
[ Laughs ]

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:54.033
Yes, sir!

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:55.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:58.367
-Also, I want to note that,
earlier I chose Haagen-Dazs

00:01:58.367 --> 00:02:00.400
for that ice cream joke,
instead of a certain

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.033
Vermont-based ice cream company,

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:03.367
which has still refused
to respond

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:04.767
to my detailed request

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:07.300
for my own personalized
ice cream flavor,

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.501
called A Closer Lick.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:11.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:13.033
[ Cheering ]
I guess, uh --

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.200
I guess our friends
at Ben &amp; Jerry's

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.133
are laugh-tose intolerant.

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:20.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:22.767
[ As Carson ] Laugh-tose,
laugh-tose intolerant.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:24.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.033
Laugh-tose intolerant.

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:27.300
Did you like that one, Wally?

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.601
-I don't want
to do this anymore.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:30.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:32.601
-Hm, when did Wally
get so choosy?

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:35.133
[ Laughter ]
Anyway, the point is

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:37.767
Biden is in Scotland
for a climate summit,

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:39.968
coming off a trip to Rome,
where, among other things,

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:41.801
he met with the Pope
for 90 minutes,

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:43.801
which, as far as anyone
can remember,

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:45.801
is the longest meeting
any sitting president

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:47.000
has had with the Pope,

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.834
especially compared
to Biden's predecessor.

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:51.734
-Tonight, President Biden
with a very busy first day

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:53.234
of his second overseas trip

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.300
ahead of the G20 Summit in Rome,

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:58.267
traveling to the Vatican,
where he had a lengthy meeting

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:00.834
with Pope Francis --
90 minutes in all.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:03.667
-When President Trump met
with the Pope,

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.133
it lasted 30 minutes.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:06.534
-I mean, I guess
it shouldn't be surprising

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.100
that Biden's meeting
with the Pope

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.634
was three times
as long as Trump's.

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:12.067
I mean, knowing Biden,
he puts in a good 40 minutes

00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:14.100
with the barista when he pops
in to Starbucks.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.634
[ As Biden ] Let's run it
through one more time

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.434
because I got to tell you,
grande and tall

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:20.100
both mean big where I come from.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.434
And Biden is
a practicing Catholic

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:25.334
and a man of deep faith,
while Trump probably thinks

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:27.367
stained glass
just needs a little Windex.

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:28.901
[ Laughter ]
I mean, I can't even begin

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:30.834
to imagine what a meeting
between Donald Trump

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.200
and Pope Francis would be about.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.334
[ As Trump ]
It's an honor to meet you,

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.367
you, Your Holiness, Mr. Pope.

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:36.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.100
Can I call you Frank?
We love religion

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.167
and we love church.

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:40.601
[ Laughter ]
We love church.

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:43.033
Don't we, Frank?
The Bible is, well,

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:44.200
it's number one, isn't it?

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.133
That's what it's all about,

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:47.634
isn't it?
Isn't it, Frank?

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.167
I like the Old Testament
and, of course,

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:50.234
the gritty reboot,

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:51.534
the New Testament.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:53.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.133
We love a reboot, don't we?

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.200
But I like the old.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.901
You know who else I like
that was old?

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:58.000
Arnold Palmer.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.434
Met him at Augusta National
in '92.

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:03.501
Stay with me, Pope.
I was there --

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:05.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:06.634
[ Fresh laughter and applause ]

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:08.167
I was there --
Do you need to translate?

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:09.901
How's his English?
I'll just plow through.

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:11.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.634
I was there.
We invented the drink.

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:14.667
He couldn't decide
between lemonade and iced tea

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:16.000
and I said, "Arnold,
why not both?"

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.200
[ Laughter ]
And they go --

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.300
they go so great together,

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.067
just like the Old
and New Testament.

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:23.167
The Pope fell asleep.

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:24.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:26.267
Someone wake up the Pope.

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:29.801
So, Biden is on a much needed
getaway, as his poll numbers sag

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:32.133
and Republicans continue
to coalesce around Trumpism

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:34.667
and the core narrative that
the 2020 election was stolen.

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:36.534
In Virginia, for example,
the governor's race there

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:38.968
is neck-and-neck, in a state
Biden won by 10 points.

00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:41.033
The GOP candidate there,
Glenn Youngkin,

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:42.767
has tried to distance
himself from Trump,

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:44.767
while also keeping
his supporters onboard,

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:47.501
a task that got trickier
when Trump announced

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:50.133
that he would hold
a tele-rally for Youngkin.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:52.033
Youngkin has said
that he has no intention

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:53.667
of participating
in the Trump rally.

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:55.100
-A lot of Republicans
would be thrilled

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.667
to be on a stage with Trump,

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:58.834
so close to Election Day.

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:01.434
Not so much in Virginia.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.501
And it sounds like Youngkin
won't even get on the phone

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:05.267
with him publicly.

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:06.734
What's happening?

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:11.934
-No, Jim, he has no plans
to participate

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:15.367
with the former president
in that tele-rally on Monday.

00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:17.434
He has long distanced himself
from Trump,

00:05:17.434 --> 00:05:19.334
but engaged Trump supporters.

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:22.133
-The former president is doing
a tele-rally on Monday.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:25.000
Will you attend and do you
welcome him to Virginia?

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.801
-Well, so I haven't been
involved in that.

00:05:27.801 --> 00:05:29.033
The teams are talking.

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:30.267
-I'm sure they would love
to have you.

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:31.334
-I know.
-Would you like to do that?

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:32.567
I'll answer you in a second.

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:33.667
I've been out campaigning.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:34.667
I'm not going to be engaged

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:35.834
in the tele town hall,

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.834
but we have more people
helping us

00:05:37.834 --> 00:05:38.834
than you can possibly believe.

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:40.133
This is about unity.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:41.300
-Yes, famously, that's what

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.934
Donald Trump is all about --
unity.

00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:44.834
[ Laughter ]
If real estate
hadn't worked out,

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:46.100
he could've been
a couples' counselor.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:47.167
"Have you tried a three-way?

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:48.567
I hear that solves
a lot of problems.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:50.334
Let me just lock the door."

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:52.133
[ Laughter ]
Trump stoked a violent
insurrection

00:05:52.133 --> 00:05:53.434
to overthrow democracy,

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:55.868
and oversaw a disastrous
response to a deadly pandemic,

00:05:55.868 --> 00:05:57.801
among many other things.
You can't thread the needle

00:05:57.801 --> 00:05:59.868
and have it both ways
by courting his supporters,

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:01.767
while also keeping him
at arm's length.

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:03.234
It's hard to say,
"If you like Trump,

00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:04.801
you'll like me,
but I don't like Trump.

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:06.968
Also, elections are rigged,
so get out there and vote."

00:06:06.968 --> 00:06:08.400
[ Laughter ]
Being a Republican

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.634
who keeps Trump at arm's length

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:11.234
is like trying
to make it 24 hours

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:13.834
without seeing any "Succession"
spoilers on social media.

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:15.033
It's not going to happen.

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:16.334
You know,
I didn't watch last night,

00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:18.067
but, thanks to Twitter,
I don't have to.

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:20.901
Look, I'm not one of those
"No spoilers" people,

00:06:20.901 --> 00:06:22.767
but just give me a day!

00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:24.634
[ Laughter ]
Yesterday was Halloween and,

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:27.300
by the time "Succession" was on,
I was passed out on the couch,

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.868
covered in Necco Wafers
and Tootsie Rolls --

00:06:29.868 --> 00:06:33.567
the only candy my kids
let me have!

00:06:33.567 --> 00:06:35.334
[ Laughter ]
I tried to sneak
one peanut butter cup

00:06:35.334 --> 00:06:36.868
out of the little one's bag
and he called me

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:38.567
a Reese's Piece of [bleep]

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:40.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:42.200
Then, he slapped my hand
so hard,

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.834
I had to write
with my left one today.

00:06:43.834 --> 00:06:46.634
Which is why the note I left you
looks like that!

00:06:46.634 --> 00:06:48.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:50.701
Most Republicans are
full-throated supporters

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:52.467
of Trump and his assault
on democracy,

00:06:52.467 --> 00:06:54.734
while others, like Youngkin,
are trying to pull off a con

00:06:54.734 --> 00:06:57.100
where they tap into Trumpism
as an ideology

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.200
and court Trump's base

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.834
without standing next
to him onstage,

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:01.734
but one reason
it'll never work is

00:07:01.734 --> 00:07:04.133
Trump always makes everything
about himself,

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:07.300
as he did yet again in response
to speculation from the press.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.934
He issued a statement insisting
that he and Glenn Youngkin

00:07:09.934 --> 00:07:11.400
are actually very good friends.

00:07:20.067 --> 00:07:22.534
Cool, I'm sure Youngkin
is thrilled to hear that.

00:07:22.534 --> 00:07:23.901
[ Laughter ]
Republicans in Virginia
have been trying

00:07:23.901 --> 00:07:25.567
to appeal to Trump's base
without getting

00:07:25.567 --> 00:07:27.234
Trump himself involved,
but he can't help it.

00:07:27.234 --> 00:07:28.501
His next statement
is going to say...

00:07:35.033 --> 00:07:36.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:37.968
Just another reminder
for Republicans --

00:07:37.968 --> 00:07:40.434
no matter how hard you try,
you can never escape Trump.

00:07:40.434 --> 00:07:42.701
You guys are like the people
who think Chucky's dead

00:07:42.701 --> 00:07:44.334
because you threw him
out a window.

00:07:44.334 --> 00:07:45.934
[ Laughter ]
"No need to look.

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:47.701
I'm sure the fall killed Chucky.

00:07:47.701 --> 00:07:50.534
Now, let's move on
from Chucky the doll

00:07:50.534 --> 00:07:52.534
and talk more
about Chucky's ideas!"

00:07:52.534 --> 00:07:56.133
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.133 --> 00:07:57.434
[ Applause ]

00:07:57.434 --> 00:07:59.734
Did the analogy get a little
too far away from us?

00:07:59.734 --> 00:08:01.701
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.701 --> 00:08:03.934
On Fox News over the weekend,
for example,

00:08:03.934 --> 00:08:05.367
Trump appeared
with Jeanine Pirro

00:08:05.367 --> 00:08:06.734
for his regular rant session,

00:08:06.734 --> 00:08:08.701
where she tried
to call him a kingmaker,

00:08:08.701 --> 00:08:10.601
but accidentally
used the wrong term.

00:08:10.601 --> 00:08:13.100
-My base has to turn out.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.334
If my base turns out,
he's going to win,

00:08:15.334 --> 00:08:16.567
and I hope they turn out.

00:08:16.567 --> 00:08:18.267
I really want them to turn out.

00:08:18.267 --> 00:08:21.634
And I think, if my base
doesn't come out, he can't win.

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:23.501
I think my base has
to come out very strongly.

00:08:23.501 --> 00:08:25.267
-Do you see yourself
as a kingpin

00:08:25.267 --> 00:08:26.601
for elections going forward?

00:08:26.601 --> 00:08:28.868
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Well, something has happened,

00:08:28.868 --> 00:08:30.601
and this is not
from an egotistical standpoint.

00:08:30.601 --> 00:08:32.467
-Yeah. I asked a question.
-It's a great honor
because it's never

00:08:32.467 --> 00:08:34.367
happened before to anybody.

00:08:34.367 --> 00:08:36.601
If I endorse somebody, they win.

00:08:36.601 --> 00:08:38.334
If I endorse somebody,
they win.

00:08:38.334 --> 00:08:40.467
I think I'm 148-2.

00:08:40.467 --> 00:08:42.467
-You can't just make up
your own win-loss record.

00:08:42.467 --> 00:08:45.934
[ Laughter ]
Otherwise, the Jets to be 7-0,
instead of 2-5.

00:08:45.934 --> 00:08:49.234
Although, the Jets
did have a big win yesterday.

00:08:49.234 --> 00:08:50.467
And, if I'm being honest,

00:08:50.467 --> 00:08:52.367
the last thing we need
at late night right now

00:08:52.367 --> 00:08:53.901
is the Jets being competitive.

00:08:53.901 --> 00:08:55.901
This is already
a pretty troubling time

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:57.167
for our writing staff,
in regards

00:08:57.167 --> 00:08:58.567
to easy New York punch lines.

00:08:58.567 --> 00:09:00.267
I mean, the Knicks are
in first place.

00:09:00.267 --> 00:09:01.634
LaGuardia's getting redone.

00:09:01.634 --> 00:09:02.767
It might be nice now.

00:09:02.767 --> 00:09:04.234
[ Laughter ]
De Blasio's leaving office.

00:09:04.234 --> 00:09:07.100
Even Pizza Rat went
on a plant-based diet

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.667
and he looks great now.

00:09:08.667 --> 00:09:11.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:19.834 --> 00:09:23.167
Here's me earlier today.

00:09:23.167 --> 00:09:25.033
"Handsome jacked rat?

00:09:25.033 --> 00:09:27.667
Exclamation point."

00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:31.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:31.234 --> 00:09:33.534
All I'm saying is
it's going to be touch-and-go

00:09:33.534 --> 00:09:36.000
until April for New York jokes,
until the Mets come back,

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.801
although, knowing the Mets,
they might not come back.

00:09:37.801 --> 00:09:39.534
Where are you guys?
It's opening day!

00:09:39.534 --> 00:09:42.200
"It is? Since when does baseball
start in April?"

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.767
Since for always!

00:09:43.767 --> 00:09:44.767
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.767 --> 00:09:46.067
Also, Jeanine, I'm pretty sure

00:09:46.067 --> 00:09:48.100
you meant to say kingmaker,
which is a good thing,

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:50.601
not kingpin, which is usually
reserved for criminals.

00:09:50.601 --> 00:09:52.868
[ Laughter ]
That's a very revealing slip.

00:09:52.868 --> 00:09:54.534
I'd say it's Freudian,
but with you,

00:09:54.534 --> 00:09:55.868
it's probably Franzian.

00:09:55.868 --> 00:09:58.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:03.234
-[ Groaning ]
-Whoo!

00:10:03.634 --> 00:10:04.701
-[ Laughing ]
Who groaned?

00:10:04.701 --> 00:10:07.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:10.167 --> 00:10:11.868
We spent a long time today
talking

00:10:11.868 --> 00:10:13.334
about a joke we're not going
to do, which is

00:10:13.334 --> 00:10:15.200
Trump being insulted
that he was called kingpin

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:18.868
because he wouldn't like
the superhero villain Kingpin.

00:10:18.868 --> 00:10:19.934
[ Laughter ]

00:10:19.934 --> 00:10:21.133
[ As Trump ]
Never caught Daredevil.

00:10:21.133 --> 00:10:23.300
[ Laughter ]

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.200
As we speak, he's still trying
to hide records

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:26.534
about what happened
on January 6th

00:10:26.534 --> 00:10:28.300
from the committee investigating
the insurrection

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:30.167
and, this weekend,
we found out more

00:10:30.167 --> 00:10:32.701
about exactly what types
of records he's trying to hide.

00:10:32.701 --> 00:10:36.000
-They include files from his
top administration officials

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:37.467
Stephen Miller,
Kayleigh McEnany,

00:10:37.467 --> 00:10:39.834
and then, White House
Chief of Staff Mark Meadows.

00:10:39.834 --> 00:10:43.133
Among Meadows' papers
are three handwritten notes

00:10:43.133 --> 00:10:46.067
specifically about the events
of January 6th.

00:10:46.067 --> 00:10:48.834
-We did not know
what records had existed

00:10:48.834 --> 00:10:51.167
in the Trump White House
before last night.

00:10:51.167 --> 00:10:52.934
In this court filing,
very late at night,

00:10:52.934 --> 00:10:55.634
the National Archives
puts out a list

00:10:55.634 --> 00:10:58.534
of more than 700 pages,
itemized, saying,

00:10:58.534 --> 00:11:01.434
"This is what Donald Trump
wants to keep secret,"

00:11:01.434 --> 00:11:04.367
and they really gave details
that we didn't know.

00:11:04.367 --> 00:11:07.033
There are these handwritten
memos, or handwritten notes

00:11:07.033 --> 00:11:08.501
from Chief of Staff
Mark Meadows,

00:11:08.501 --> 00:11:10.467
specifically about January 6th.

00:11:10.467 --> 00:11:14.300
There are call logs
and switchboard call logs

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:18.067
about calls to President Trump,
to Vice President Mike Pence,

00:11:18.067 --> 00:11:20.434
leading up to,
about January 6th.

00:11:20.434 --> 00:11:21.767
These are
very specific things --

00:11:21.767 --> 00:11:24.901
White House visitor logs,
White House call records.

00:11:24.901 --> 00:11:26.667
-Personally, I'm shocked
the Trump White House

00:11:26.667 --> 00:11:28.234
even had any records at all.

00:11:28.234 --> 00:11:30.767
I assumed that place was like
a Radio Shack in a zombie movie.

00:11:30.767 --> 00:11:33.200
[ Laughter ]
Most of the call logs
probably just say...

00:11:35.167 --> 00:11:38.133
[ Laughter ]

00:11:38.133 --> 00:11:39.601
[ Applause ]
And there's an obvious reason

00:11:39.601 --> 00:11:41.367
Trump wants to keep
those records hidden,

00:11:41.367 --> 00:11:42.534
as we've discussed before.

00:11:42.534 --> 00:11:44.167
Trump and his cronies
had a detailed plan

00:11:44.167 --> 00:11:45.701
for overturning election results

00:11:45.701 --> 00:11:48.567
and they tried to execute that
plan and they almost succeeded.

00:11:48.567 --> 00:11:51.467
It wasn't an impulse or a whim,
it was a plot.

00:11:51.467 --> 00:11:53.834
Trump even had a lawyer
who wrote an instruction manual

00:11:53.834 --> 00:11:55.200
for overturning the result.

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:56.801
When Vice President Mike Pence
declined

00:11:56.801 --> 00:11:58.267
to follow through on the plan,

00:11:58.267 --> 00:12:00.133
that same Trump lawyer
told Pence

00:12:00.133 --> 00:12:02.100
the violent insurrection
was his fault,

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:04.434
as the insurrection
was happening.

00:12:04.434 --> 00:12:06.400
-The Washington Post
is now reporting that,

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:08.934
in the middle
of the Capitol invasion,

00:12:08.934 --> 00:12:11.567
as rioters were overrunning
the building

00:12:11.567 --> 00:12:13.968
and chanting "Hang Mike Pence,"

00:12:13.968 --> 00:12:16.801
one of former President Trump's
attorneys emailed

00:12:16.801 --> 00:12:19.934
a top aide
for the then-vice president,

00:12:19.934 --> 00:12:22.133
blaming Pence for the violence

00:12:22.133 --> 00:12:25.701
because he refused to block
the election certification.

00:12:25.701 --> 00:12:27.834
-And, when that aide described
the attack

00:12:27.834 --> 00:12:29.934
as a siege in an email,

00:12:29.934 --> 00:12:32.801
Trump attorney John Eastman
wrote back...

00:12:44.267 --> 00:12:46.634
Eastman essentially
blaming Pence

00:12:46.634 --> 00:12:49.033
for what happened
on January 6th.

00:12:49.033 --> 00:12:51.367
-Even as the rioters are
rampaging through the Capitol,

00:12:51.367 --> 00:12:53.701
threatening to kill Mike Pence,
one of Trump's cronies

00:12:53.701 --> 00:12:56.334
was still pushing Pence
to overturn the result.

00:12:56.334 --> 00:12:58.701
It's like telling a Walmart
greeter to stand their post,

00:12:58.701 --> 00:13:01.200
even as a mob
of Black Friday shoppers storms

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:02.400
through the front doors.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:04.734
"Hello! Welcome to Walmart.
Happy shopping!

00:13:04.734 --> 00:13:07.400
Help me! I need backup!
I'm under siege!

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.534
I need extraction, you know!
Oh, crap!

00:13:09.534 --> 00:13:11.434
Oh, this is just
a happy face button!"

00:13:11.434 --> 00:13:13.033
[ Laughter ]

00:13:13.033 --> 00:13:15.434
But that's because the big lie
that the election was stolen

00:13:15.434 --> 00:13:17.434
and the idea that the
insurrection was justified

00:13:17.434 --> 00:13:20.000
are now a key part of Trumpism
and the core of the modern GOP

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:21.934
and, no matter how hard
they try,

00:13:21.934 --> 00:13:24.100
the Glenn Youngkins of the world
can't run away from that.

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:26.601
Last week, far-right crazy
person Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:13:26.601 --> 00:13:29.033
[ Laughter ]
even suggested that
the insurrection was justified

00:13:29.033 --> 00:13:30.767
by the Declaration
of Independence.

00:13:30.767 --> 00:13:33.501
-But the real truth is
the communist revolution

00:13:33.501 --> 00:13:35.901
that the Democrats funded
and waged

00:13:35.901 --> 00:13:38.334
every single day
and every single night

00:13:38.334 --> 00:13:41.000
in American cities
all across our country,

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.367
you see, that was an attack
on innocent American people,

00:13:44.367 --> 00:13:47.934
whereas, January 6th was just
a riot at the Capitol.

00:13:47.934 --> 00:13:49.067
And, if you think about what

00:13:49.067 --> 00:13:51.234
our Declaration
of Independence says,

00:13:51.234 --> 00:13:54.100
it says to overthrow tyrants.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:56.334
-I don't know.
You think Democrats are tyrants?

00:13:56.334 --> 00:13:58.000
Have you ever even seen
Chuck Schumer?

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.601
Tyrants don't wear their glasses
that far down on their nose.

00:14:00.601 --> 00:14:02.467
[ Laughter ]
It's like he's staring at a menu

00:14:02.467 --> 00:14:04.367
at a diner on the
Upper West Side for three hours.

00:14:04.367 --> 00:14:06.300
[ As Schumer ]
We're very close
to coming to agreement

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:07.667
on whether to split
an appetizer.

00:14:07.667 --> 00:14:10.300
"Sir, the restaurant
is closing very soon."

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:11.334
[ Laughter ]
[ As Schumer ] Okay, okay, well,

00:14:11.334 --> 00:14:12.567
just leave me here in the dark.

00:14:12.567 --> 00:14:14.033
I've got a New York Times
crossword puzzle

00:14:14.033 --> 00:14:15.834
I've been working on since 1985.

00:14:15.834 --> 00:14:17.167
[ Laughter ]

00:14:17.167 --> 00:14:19.200
The GOP has embraced Trumpism
fully and completely,

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:21.534
whether they brag about it
or whether they try to play coy.

00:14:21.534 --> 00:14:23.901
He sowed a violent insurrection
to overthrow democracy,

00:14:23.901 --> 00:14:25.367
but Republicans
are still onboard,

00:14:25.367 --> 00:14:27.167
which means he'll almost
certainly try

00:14:27.167 --> 00:14:28.434
to do it again, making him a...

00:14:28.434 --> 00:14:30.400
-Kingpin for elections
going forward?

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:32.634
[ Laughter and applause ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

